{"title":"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems\">2015 AMC 12A #7</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems\">2015 AMC 10A #9</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two right circular cylinders have the same volume. The radius of the second cylinder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> more than the radius of the first. What is the relationship between the heights of the two cylinders?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53dacea99e1e2ba98f25bf6cf21431f4fedbb92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{The second height is } 10\\% \\text{ less than the first.} \\\\ \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{The first height is } 10\\% \\text{ more than the second.} \\\\ \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{The second height is } 21\\% \\text{ less than the first.} \\\\ \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{The first height is } 21\\% \\text{ more than the second.} \\\\ \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{The second height is } 80\\% \\text{ of the first.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"99\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the radius of the first cylinder be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and the radius of the second cylinder be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. Also, let the height of the first cylinder be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d78aae1741ff43c6f40e2077f1ab67900cca2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and the height of the second cylinder be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ec781a0e6836ea5e030a44927477cfd5560fecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. We are told <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/41704dff30bf2daea06efcba03fdcd72cb507478.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_2=\\frac{11r_1}{10}\\]\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/177bac559181a4d8c72c9057a70337eabab64b2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\pi r_1^2h_1=\\pi r_2^2h_2\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" /> Substituting the first equation into the second and dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3ff9714fedab21b6406945de393a33855a715f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_1^2h_1=\\frac{121r_1^2}{100}h_2\\implies h_1=\\frac{121h_2}{100}.\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"39\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/0646f7cddc13e6f3bf3707b8bc43d9bf0b3a3651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{The first height is } 21\\% \\text{ more than the second.}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"382\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fx7bYbysB24\">https://youtu.be/fx7bYbysB24</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zVCHWxfKErE\">https://youtu.be/zVCHWxfKErE</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A\">2015 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a>